      "text": "Ken French's ST_Rev factor is the average of the two low-prior-return portfolios minus the average of the two high-prior-return portfolios: ST_Rev = \u00bd(Small Lo + Big Lo) \u2212 \u00bd(Small Hi + Big Hi). The script uses only the first section of the file (value-weighted monthly returns) and stops at the first non-monthly line, so it does not mix in the later sections. I have not run it against the full file.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\nrows = []\nstarted = False\nwith open(\"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_1_0.csv\", \"r\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n    for line in f:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(\",\")]\n        if parts and re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0]) and len(parts) >= 7:\n            started = True\n            rows.append(parts[:7])\n        elif started:\n            break\n\ndf = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"date\", \"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"])\ndf[\"date\"] = df[\"date\"].astype(int)\nfor c in df.columns[1:]:\n    df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\")\n    df.loc[df[c] <= -99.0, c] = np.nan\n\ndf[\"value\"] = 0.5 * (df[\"SL\"] + df[\"BL\"]) - 0.5 * (df[\"SH\"] + df[\"BH\"])\nout = df[[\"date\", \"value\"]].dropna()\nout.to_csv(\"output.csv\", index=False)\n```",
